A||||5||88CoupeV6||New found power||||10||
Z||000000||88CoupeV6||11-14-2001||04:03 PM||||Today I changed the fuel filter on my 88 GT. It was like a rustbucket. It was still the factory one I think. It had to be pried out. I should have changed it when I got the car this summer. I can't believe a car with 160,000 never had it changed. Just like the sparkplugs. I changed them when I got the car and the 3 back ones were the factory ones. I am surprised the car ran they were so bad. It feels like it has more power now.<BR>What is with some people?<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Raydar||11-14-2001||04:18 PM||||Some people don't change stuff until it just won't run any more.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||11-14-2001||04:30 PM||||When I put a new pump and filter on my 88, the filter was the original one. 185,000 miles! I tried to blow through it with an air hose and it was almost impossible- I cut the case open just to see what it looked like and the filter paper had fossilized and turned into a little pleated stone.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jaygee79||11-14-2001||06:56 PM||||at least it wasn't as bad as the one in my grandfather's sable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||pHoOl||11-14-2001||07:29 PM||||Where is the fuel filter located?  I've been wondering about changing mine.. but i was afraid that somehow it was inside the tank like the pump.  Just curious if this is something that i can change in the apartment parking lot, or if i'll have to wait until i'm at home and jack it up<P>------------------<BR>Kills:<BR>97 Neon R/T<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>         <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||11-14-2001||07:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pHoOl:<BR><B>Where is the fuel filter located?  I've been wondering about changing mine.. but i was afraid that somehow it was inside the tank like the pump.  Just curious if this is something that i can change in the apartment parking lot, or if i'll have to wait until i'm at home and jack it up<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The fuel filter is located on the engine side of the gas tank. I had to use a jack (and jackstands) to get under there and change it. Remember to relieve the pressure from the valve before you do this. Or, I think you can just pull the fuel pump fuse, and start the car, then it will run out. And you'll need a container for some of the remaining fuel to drain in.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigsqoach2.gif">              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">               <BR>^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><LI>86 SC 2.5L 5spd</FONT>||||reg||1
